  "release_notes": "New Features\n- Clip sounds: add .mp3, .ogg, .flac, .m4a and more. Added sounds stay in the list (X removes one), can be trimmed with the new slider, and Stop ends a preview.\n- Rename a clip by typing in the editor's title. Its copies, exports and saved edit follow.\n- Copy puts a clip or export on the clipboard, ready to paste into Discord.\n- Drag a clip from the list into the Full Editor to add its picture and sound as new tracks.\n- Clip list: search by name or game, and a Status filter (Not Exported, Edited, Exported, Exported Video), with a status tag on each clip.\n- Clip list: Game filter has Not Detected, Show Exports hides exported videos, filters are remembered, the filter button hides them, and the list can be resized by dragging its edge.\n\nImprovements\n- A clip's size sits on its thumbnail beside its length.\n- Export As suggests the clip's name with its size (e.g. -1080p60).\n- The Full Editor imports .ts videos.\n- Float .wav clip sounds play at your volume on Windows, not full volume.\n- Uninstall also checks OBS's own recording paths before deleting anything.\n\nFixes\n- A clip stays marked as exported after its export is deleted, and one reset to how it came isn't marked as edited.\n- Bug reports sent from an error popup include the error, and show on GitHub exactly as typed.",
